Done. Summary of the P2.5 slice:

**Finding (the validation caught a real defect):** `document-search-provider.service.ts` queried `getRepository('document')` with **no** `RolePermissionConfig`. That resolves to empty object permissions + `shouldBypassPermissionChecks:false`, so `validateOperationIsPermittedOrThrow` denied select on the non-system `document` object — every caller silently got a caught `PERMISSION_DENIED` and an empty "A2E Documents" group. The provider was un-stubbed but effectively dead.

**Fix:** resolve the caller role permission config from the ambient `getWorkspaceContext()` (same seam `SearchService` uses) and pass it to `getRepository`. No bypass, ambient context stays the only workspace source.

**Tests:**
- Unit (`document-search-provider.service.spec.ts`): caller role → `intersectionOf`, no-role → fail-closed, no bypass, ambient-workspace scoping ignoring caller `workspaceId`, ILIKE escaping, mapping. 8/8.
- Tier-1 integration (`search-caller-permissions.integration-spec.ts`, new): seeded "Object-restricted" member never gets rocket titles but still finds a readable pet; a YCombinator member never sees Apple titles and finds its own. 5/5.

**Checks:** search unit 4 suites/18; tsgo exit 0; oxlint 0/0; oxfmt clean; no PLAN.md/locale/commit.

**Not ticked:** document-provider validation through the `searchAppRecords` GraphQL path needs a2e-documents installed (Tier 2/app-install harness); cross-workspace document leg is unit-only.

Reports appended to `docs/plan/phases/phase-02-report.md` and `.ralph-tui/progress.md`.

